{"text": "UNITED STATES ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION AGENCY\nSHINGTON D\n\nJUL 26 2019\n\nMs. Emma Best\nMuckRock News\n411A Highland Avenue\nSomerville, MA 02144\n\nRE: Request Number EPA-HQ-2019-006496\nDear Ms. Best:\n\nThis letter concerns the above-referenced Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) request,\nreceived by the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) Freedom of Information Office in\nwhich you are secking records containing 50 non-case sensitive words that were sent to and from\nEPA offices between January 1, 2018 and the present.\n\nYour request does not reasonably describe the records you are seeking in a way that will\npermit EPA employees to identify and locate them. The EPA\u2018s FOIA regulations explain:\n\n\u201cWhenever possible, your request should include specific information about each record\nsought, such as the title or name, author, recipient, and subject matter. If known, you\nshould include any file designations or descriptions for the records that you want. The\nmore specific you are about the records or type of records that you wani, the more likely\nEPA will be able to identify and locate records responsive to your request.\u201d 40 CER. \u00a7\n2.102(\u20ac).\n\nWe would like to provide you the opportunity to clarify the records that you are seeking\nso that EPA can process your request. As indicated in 40 C.E.R. \u00a7 2.102(c), please include any\nspecific information about the records you seek, including definition of director's office,\nprogram, region, or names of people to search. Additionally, the FOIA does not require federal\nagencies to respond to questions so please consider that as you are modifying your request.\n\nSince you have not provided a telephone number we are unable to connect with you\ndirectly. Please contact Monica Lewis via email at Lewis.Monica@epa.gov with your",
